// Takes what is lying in an outbox and goes.
//
// **The first creature that attacks the chain rather than the
// structure**, which is the whole reason it exists. The four kinds that
// shipped before it all converge on the tower and bite it, so every
// threat in the game was answerable the same two ways: shoot it, or mend
// what it broke. A crow damages nothing. It lands on a room's outbox,
// takes what is in it, and leaves — and the loss is a morning's harvest,
// which repair cannot put back and defence can prevent
// (`SYSTEMS.md` §5.5).
//
// Tone: this is a bird doing what birds do to an unguarded crop. It is
// not raiding you and it does not want a fight; it wants the bamboo.
// A tower that shoots one has decided its harvest is worth more than a
// bird, which is a decision rather than a duty.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
EnemyDef(
    id: "enemy.glean_crow",
    name: "Glean-crow",
    glyph: "🐦",
    // Fragile. A dart battery two-shots a skitter at 30; a crow goes
    // down to one. What makes it a problem is arriving, not surviving.
    hp: 14,
    // The fastest thing in the pack by half again — it is in and away
    // before a battery has reloaded, which is what makes *having* the
    // battery matter more than aiming it.
    speed_paces_per_100_ticks: 105,
    // Nominal, and nearly irrelevant: a crow's bite is 1 against a
    // panel's 150. What it takes is the point, and the taking is
    // modelled as the theft in `siege.rs` rather than as damage.
    damage: 1,
    attack_ticks: 45,
    // Barely two bites' worth of grip. It is not here to stay.
    cling_ticks: 90,
    // Down onto a deck, the way a leaper does. Height is exposure, and
    // an outbox on the roof is an outbox a bird can see.
    approach: Canopy,
    // Cheap, so a wave that fields crows fields several.
    threat: 8,
    // A quarter of provocation_max. A quiet tower keeps its harvest;
    // one that has been stripping the terrain has been noticed by
    // something that eats.
    min_provocation: 250,
    // Takes rather than breaks. Nothing it does needs mending, and what
    // it costs is a morning's work sitting in an outbox somebody had not
    // got to yet.
    steals: true,
)
